  <data name="Label19.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Lead applied to shift speeds and/or rpms. Values range from 0 to 10. 0 being no lead, 10
 being an insane amout of lead. Used for giving lazy or tied tranmissions time to shift, cars
 with high amounts of power with extreme rpm per second accelleration rates, or giving 
6Lxx transmissions time to do thier preshift preperations like clutch pack preloading. A
value of 2 is typical for normal 6Lxx stuff. 3-4 is normal of higher HP 6Lxx cars and trucks.</value></data>
